---
import GameLayout from "../../../layouts/GameLayout.astro";
import { ConnectionInfo } from "@/components/ConnectionInfo";
---

<GameLayout title="OverTheWire: Natas" gameName="natas">
    <h1 class="text-[30pt] font-normal leading-[1.2em] mb-4">Natas</h1>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        Natas teaches the basics of serverside web-security.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-[14pt] font-bold mt-4 mb-2">About Natas</h3>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        Each level of natas consists of its own website located at
        <strong>http://natasX.natas.labs.overthewire.org</strong>, where X is
        the level number. There is <strong>no SSH login</strong>. To access a
        level, enter the username for that level (e.g. natas0 for level 0) and
        its password.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">
        Each level has access to the password of the next level. Your job is to
        somehow obtain that next password and level up. <strong
            >All passwords are also stored in /etc/natas_webpass/</strong
        >. E.g. the password for natas5 is stored in the file
        /etc/natas_webpass/natas5 and only readable by natas4 and natas5.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-[24px] mb-4">Start here:</p>

    <ConnectionInfo
        client:load
        username="natas0"
        password="natas0"
        url="http://natas0.natas.labs.overthewire.org"
    />

    <div class="mt-8 text-sm text-[#999]">
        This wargame was developed in association with the <a
            href="http://www.nessos-project.eu/"
            class="text-[#999] underline hover:text-[#ccc]"
            >NESSoS FP7 project</a
        >.
    </div>
</GameLayout>
